# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites
# every text file to CRLF on checkout. The repository has always stored LF, so
# that leaves the working tree at odds with prettier's endOfLine: 'lf' and
# produces a "Delete ␍" error on effectively every line of every file.
#
# eol=lf pins the *working tree* to LF as well, and takes precedence over
# whatever core.autocrlf a given clone happens to have.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize or diff as text.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
